    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "How many ways can five adults and two children be arranged so that the children are separated by at least one adult?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3600$\n\nSubtract arrangements with the children together from all arrangements.",
      "worked": "There are $7!$ unrestricted arrangements. With the two children together, there are six objects to arrange, and the children can swap positions within their group.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=7!-6!\\times2!\\\\N&=5040-1440\\\\N&=3600.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
